+# Getting this work onto GitHub
+
+## The situation
+
+Nothing here has been pushed. Remote git is disabled in this session, and the
+sandbox resets its git history almost every turn — six times so far. Each reset
+discards commits and keeps the working tree, which is why the work survives.
+
+The important realisation: **the upload restriction you hit is the platform's
+attachment filter, not GitHub's.** So the work does not need another coding
+session at all. It can go through your own GitHub access directly.
+
+## The package
+
+| File | Size | Contents |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `transfer/kryptos-work-complete.zip` | **620 KB** | Everything, generated pages included. Extract over a clone and commit — no build step. **Start here.** |
+| `transfer/kryptos-work-files.zip` | 399 KB | Source only; the 50 wiki pages and app data get rebuilt by scripts. |
+| `transfer/kryptos-work-source-only.patch(.txt)` | 462 KB | Same as above, as a diff. |
+| `transfer/parts/patch-part-00…05.txt` | 6 × ~88 KB | The patch split, if something imposes a size cap. |
+
+Paths inside the zips are repo-relative, so extracting on top of a clone lands
+every file in the right place.
+
+**Verified, not assumed.** `kryptos-work-files.zip` was extracted over a clean
+checkout of `main`: 50 ciphers register, Kryptos K1 decrypts correctly, and all
+**281 tests pass**. `kryptos-work-complete.zip` additionally carries the 50 wiki
+pages, 3 history articles and the 14 verified Kryptos app entries, and passes
+the browser suite 19/19 with no build step.
+
+---
+
+## Route 1 — GitHub in the browser (no local tools, no new session)
+
+1. Download `transfer/kryptos-work-complete.zip` from this session's file
+   viewer and unzip it on your machine.
+2. Open the repository on github.com and press <kbd>.</kbd> — this opens
+   **github.dev**, a full editor in the browser.
+3. Drag the unzipped folders into the file explorer on the left. Confirm
+   overwrites when asked.
+4. Open the Source Control panel, write a commit message, commit, and sync.
+
+Nothing is installed and nothing else is uploaded; the browser talks
+straight to GitHub.
+
+## Route 2 — a local clone (fastest if you have git)
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/ahardkore/Buttcrack---Cipher-Breaker.git
+cd Buttcrack---Cipher-Breaker
+unzip -o ~/Downloads/kryptos-work-complete.zip
+git add -A
+git commit -m "Kryptos work: 50 ciphers, verified app data, cipher wiki, manuscript"
+git push origin main          # or push a branch and open a PR
+```
+
+With the source-only zip or the patch, add the rebuild step first:
+
+```bash
+python3 ventures/cipher-solver-web/build_pages.py
+python3 scripts/build_kryptos_app_data.py
+python3 scripts/build_site.py --out _site
+```
+
+## Route 3 — copy-paste, if you cannot download anything
+
+Create the new files through **Add file → Create new file** on github.com and
+paste each one's contents from the viewer. The eleven new files, most valuable
+first:
+
+| Lines | File |
+| --- | --- |
+| 1574 | `buttcrack/ciphers/keyed.py` |
+| 614 | `ventures/cipher-solver-web/wiki_ciphers.py` |
+| 396 | `ventures/cipher-solver-web/wiki_history.py` |
+| 280 | `scripts/build_kryptos_app_data.py` |
+| 278 | `buttcrack/ciphers/matrix.py` |
+| 146 | `scripts/bench_layers.py` |
+| 93 | `scripts/sumclock_corpus_scan.py` |
+| 93 | `scripts/kryptos_ctf.py` |
+
+`keyed.py` alone carries the Kryptos capability — it reproduces the sculpture's
+K1 and breaks PK1 and PK3. Edits to existing files (`engine.py`,
+`transposition.py`, `polygraphic.py`, `codes.py`, the tests) would still be
+missing by this route, so the six-deep layered search and the newer ciphers
+would not come across.
+
+---
+
+## Check it arrived
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .   # 281 tests, 6 skipped
+python3 -m buttcrack selftest --quick        # 142/142 checks
+python3 -m buttcrack ciphers | head -1       # "50 ciphers, codes and encodings"
+node ventures/cipher-solver-web/test.js      # 19/19
+python3 scripts/kryptos_ctf.py --budget 150 --only PK1,PK2,PK3   # 3/3
+```
+
+## What is in it
+
+* **Solver** — 50 ciphers, up from 36. Quagmire III and sum-clocks over keyed
+  alphabets, Hill with a row-separable attack, four-square, trifid, Myszkowski,
+  AMSCO, Porta, and six new peelable layers. Six-deep layered search, including
+  cipher-on-cipher chains.
+* **Kryptos** — reproduces the sculpture's K1 and K2 from the published keys,
+  and breaks Paradigm Kryptos PK1, PK2 and PK3 from ciphertext alone. Crib
+  algebra, the sum-clock annihilator, and a corpus scanner.
+* **Site** — a wiki page for every cipher, generated from the registry, plus
+  three history articles.
+* **Honesty fixes** — the Kryptos app was showing seven fabricated ciphertexts;
+  its data is now generated and verified at build time. The manuscript's
+  claimed PK9 and PK10 solutions are retracted, with the evidence.
+
+## A warning for whoever picks this up
+
+Do not trust a commit in this sandbox to persist. Write files and check them
+back. The pattern, six times running: the commit succeeds, and by the next turn
+`HEAD` is back at the PR #6 merge with the work sitting as uncommitted changes.
+The files have survived every time; the commits have not.
