++# Moving this work into a new coding session
++
++## Why it isn't showing
++
++Nothing in this session was ever pushed to GitHub. A new coding session starts
++from a **fresh clone of GitHub**, so it sees `origin/main` (currently the merge
++of PR #7) and none of the work done here.
++
++Two separate things were going on:
++
++1. **Remote operations are disabled in this session** — its pull request was
++   already merged, so `git push` and `gh` cannot reach GitHub from here.
++2. **This sandbox's git history keeps being reset.** The reflog shows a fresh
++   clone followed by a checkout, with no other entries, so commits made here
++   have repeatedly disappeared. The *files* survive each reset — they simply
++   come back as uncommitted changes in the working tree.
++
++So the work exists, in full, as files. It just has no route to GitHub from
++inside this session.
++
++## What the work is
++
++116 files, ~13,300 insertions against `origin/main`:
++
++| Area | Files |
++| --- | --- |
++| Solver: new ciphers and attacks | `buttcrack/ciphers/keyed.py`, `matrix.py`, `transposition.py`, `polygraphic.py`, `codes.py`, `encodings.py`, `shift.py`, `polyalphabetic.py`, `__init__.py` |
++| Solver: layered search, scoring honesty | `buttcrack/engine.py`, `buttcrack/results.py`, `buttcrack/detect.py`, `buttcrack/cli.py`, `buttcrack/server.py`, `buttcrack/selftest.py` |
++| Kryptos work | `scripts/kryptos_ctf.py`, `scripts/build_kryptos_app_data.py`, `scripts/sumclock_corpus_scan.py`, `kryptos-app/*`, `kryptos/THE_KRYPTOS_DECRYPTION_MANUSCRIPT.md`, status banners on 11 research docs |
++| Site: cipher wiki and history | `ventures/cipher-solver-web/wiki_ciphers.py`, `wiki_history.py`, `build_pages.py`, `style.css`, plus 49 generated pages |
++| Tests and benchmarks | `tests/test_ciphers.py`, `tests/test_engine.py`, `scripts/bench_layers.py` |
++
++## How to move it
++
++The patch is committed at **`transfer/kryptos-work-source-only.patch`**, inside
++the repository. That location is deliberate: this sandbox has been observed to
++reset git history and to discard files written outside the repository, while
++files *inside* it survive. So the patch travels with the working tree.
++
++Regenerate the other two forms any time with:
++
++```bash
++git bundle create transfer/kryptos-work.bundle origin/main..HEAD   # keeps history
++git diff origin/main..HEAD > transfer/kryptos-work.patch           # everything
++```
++
++### Option 1 — a bundle (best: keeps history)
++
++Regenerate it with the command above. A bundle is a real git repository in one file.
++
++```bash
++# in the new session, at the repo root
++git bundle verify /path/to/kryptos-work.bundle
++git pull /path/to/kryptos-work.bundle HEAD
++git push origin HEAD           # works there; GitHub auth is wired in
++```
++
++### Option 2 — the full patch
++
++Regenerate with the command above; about 1 MB, every changed file including
++generated pages.
++
++```bash
++git apply --3way /path/to/kryptos-work.patch
++git add -A && git commit -m "Kryptos work"
++git push origin HEAD
++```
++
++### Option 3 — source only, then rebuild (smallest)
++
++`transfer/kryptos-work-source-only.patch` (462 KB, committed) omits everything a
++build script regenerates: the 49 generated wiki pages, `sitemap.xml`, and
++`kryptos-app/data.js`. **This is the one to use.** Delete the file after the
++transfer; it is an aid, not part of the project.
